# DBW LEAD CARD FORMAT SKILL

## PURPOSE
This skill owns all HTML formatting for DBW daily
lead delivery emails. When called, it receives
structured lead data and outputs a complete HTML
email body ready to insert into a Gmail draft.
The calling task does zero formatting — it only
collects data and passes it here.

## INPUTS REQUIRED
Pass all of the following before calling this skill.
Use the label Not found for any field that could
not be verified rather than leaving it blank.

For the email header, pass one time for the whole
email: rep name and nickname, today's date, states
and city clusters being worked, number of leads,
market cluster summary sentence, blade profile for
this market, call theme sentence, and data source.

For the shared market intel block, pass one time:
ready-mix and concrete suppliers found, supply
houses found, equipment rental companies found,
and DOT activity description with corridor name-drop.

For each of the five lead cards pass: company name
and city and state, full address, phone, website,
company type, revenue estimate, employee count,
year founded or years in operation, NAICS code,
company insight paragraph, all contacts with name
and title and mobile and direct and email, Sage
last invoice date if known, blade angle paragraph,
company-specific buying signals paragraph, REED
project intel block, local suppliers list with city
and state and phone, V1 and V2 and V3 opening lines
fully written out, and field read recommendation.

## HTML OUTPUT SPECIFICATION
Generate a complete HTML document using inline
styles only. No external stylesheets. No JavaScript.
Gmail strips anything that is not inline so every
style must be written directly on each element.
Use a max-width of 900px centered on the page.
Font family for all text: Arial, sans-serif.

SECTION A — EMAIL HEADER
Full-width div, background #000000, padding 24px.
Rep name and date in bold 26px color #FFD700.
Territory and market clusters in 13px #FFD700.
Blade profile and call theme in 12px italic #B8A000.
Data source note in 11px #888888.

SECTION B — SAGE WARNING BANNER
Full-width div, background #CC0000, padding 14px 18px.
Warning triangle symbol followed by bold white 13px
text: IMPORTANT — READ BEFORE YOU DIAL:
Below in regular white 12px: these leads must be
cross-referenced in Sage before calling, check for
existing accounts, open orders, prior relationships,
or assigned reps, do not call an active account
without checking first, Sage check is mandatory,
no exceptions.

SECTION C — MARKET CLUSTER OVERVIEW
Full-width div, background #1B5E20, padding 16px.
Bold white 14px header: TODAY'S MARKET CLUSTER —
ZoomInfo VERIFIED — SAME METRO, SAME TRADE.
Metro cluster details and blade profile and call
theme in 12px white. Data source in 11px #A5D6A7.

SECTION D — SHARED MARKET INTEL TABLE
Full-width div, background #E8F5E9, padding 16px.
Title in bold dark green #1B5E20 at 13px.
Full-width table with light gray borders #CCCCCC
and cell padding 8px 12px.
Include exactly four rows and no others.
Row one: Ready-Mix and Concrete.
Row two: Supply Houses.
Row three: Equipment Rental.
Row four: DOT Activity.
Left column bold #2E7D32 at 12px.
Right column black at 12px.
Do not add any other rows. Do not include blade
dealers, brands in market, pricing intel, or
competitor information under any circumstances.

SECTION E — LEAD CARDS
Repeat the following structure for all five leads.
Separate each card with a horizontal rule #CCCCCC.

LEAD CARD HEADER: full-width div, background #0D1B2A,
padding 14px 18px, white bold 15px showing lead
number and company name and city and state.

COMPANY DATA GRID: white background, border #DDDDDD,
four columns by two rows. Row one: Address, Phone,
Website, Company Type. Row two: Revenue, Employees,
Founded, NAICS. Labels bold #555555 at 11px, values
black at 12px.

COMPANY INSIGHT BLOCK: left border 4px solid #FF6F00,
background #FFF3E0, padding 12px 16px. Bold #FF6F00
label: Company Insight: followed by the specific
insight paragraph in black 12px. Must describe what
the company does, how long they have operated, what
project types they run, and why they are a strong
blade prospect. Never use generic filler text.

KEY CONTACTS TABLE: header background #1A237E, white
bold header text at 12px. Columns: Name, Title,
Mobile, Direct, Email. Alternating rows white and
#F5F5F5. Append ZI in bold green #2E7D32 after any
mobile number sourced from ZoomInfo. Show a centered
dash for any field not found.

SAGE CHECK BLOCK: left border 4px solid #CC0000,
background #FFEBEE, padding 12px 16px. Bold red
label: SAGE CHECK REQUIRED BEFORE CALLING.
Three checkbox lines:
[ ] New Account 36 plus months — 25 percent commission
[ ] Reactivation 18 to 36 months — standard rate
[ ] Active Account — pass to current rep blank line
One line below: Last Invoice Date: blank line.

BLADE ANGLE BLOCK: left border 4px solid #2E7D32,
background #F1F8E9, padding 12px 16px. Bold green
label: Blade Angle: followed by specific blade types
and sizes this contractor needs based on their trade
and equipment. Distinguish walk-behind from ride-on
if signals exist. Include reorder cycle assessment
if the data supports it. No generic filler.

BUYING SIGNALS BLOCK: left border 4px solid #1565C0,
background #E3F2FD, padding 12px 16px. Bold blue
label: Company-Specific Buying Signals: followed by
specific signals indicating active blade purchasing.
Reference DOT contracts, active projects, ZoomInfo
scoops, or growth signals. No filler.

REED PROJECT INTEL BLOCK: left border 4px solid
#B71C1C, background #FCE4EC, padding 12px 16px.
Bold dark red label: REED Project Intel: followed
by the full REED output. If a verified project was
found, show project name, awarding authority, award
date, PWD name, and complete bidder list. If no
project was found, show the DOT corridor name-drop
angle and PWD name if available.

LOCAL SUPPLIERS BLOCK: left border 4px solid #6A1B9A,
background #F3E5F5, padding 12px 16px. Bold purple
label: Local Suppliers likely buying from: followed
by a bulleted list showing supplier name, city,
state, and phone. Real businesses only. 2 to 4
suppliers per lead card.

OPENING LINES BLOCK: left border 4px solid #E65100,
background #FFF8E1, padding 12px 16px. Bold orange
label: Opening Lines: followed by all three versions.

V1 AGGRESSIVE in bold #CC0000 with italic gray use-when
note. Full script with all blanks filled in using
real data from this lead card.

V2 MIDWEST in bold #1565C0 with italic gray use-when
note. Full script with all blanks filled in.

V3 SHORTCUT in bold #2E7D32 with italic gray use-when
note. Full script with all blanks filled in.

FIELD READ in bold black: one sentence explaining
which version fits this contact and why based on
what is known about their role and personality.

CALL LOG FOOTER: background #F5F5F5, padding 10px 16px,
border top 1px solid #CCCCCC. Text in #555555 at 11px:
Called: blank | Reached: YES / NO / VM |
Follow-up date: blank.

## OUTPUT RULES
Return only valid HTML with all styles inline.
Do not return markdown. Do not wrap in code blocks.
Do not include any text outside the HTML document.
Every field passed in must appear in the output.
Never add sections not specified above.
Never omit sections that are specified above.
If a passed value is Not found, render it as a
centered dash in tables or the words Not found in
paragraph blocks so the rep knows to investigate.